JavaScript Notes for Students
-------------------------------------------------

1. JavaScript is a web programming language.
2. JavaScript is used to add functionality , interactivity to a webpage.
3. JavaScript was developed by Brendan Eich and released in 1995.
History:
Mocha → LiveScript → JavaScript → ECMAScript (ES)

4. JavaScript is a case-sensitive language.


Example: a and A are different.

5. No special software is required to start learning JavaScript. A text editor and a web browser are sufficient.
   - Chrome → V8
   - Firefox → SpiderMonkey
   - Internet Explorer → Chakra
6. JavaScript is used in different environments.

   a) Client-side (browser)

   b) Server-side (Node.js)

   c) Database-related environments (MongoDB)

7. The JavaScript file extension is .js.


 Uses of Client-Side JavaScript
 ----------------------------------
 
1. To validate forms before submission.
2. To add content dynamically to a webpage.
3. To perform calculations on a webpage.
4. To fetch data from APIs.
5. To add functionality to a webpage.
6. To respond to user actions.
7. To implement searching and filtering.
8. To show and hide webpage elements.


How many ways write the js code
--------------------------------------
JavaScript code can be written in 3 ways.

1. Inline JavaScript
Writing JavaScript code directly inside an HTML element using an event attribute.

<button class="btn btn-success" onclick="alert('hello js')">Click</button>

2. Internal JavaScript
Writing JavaScript inside the <script> tag in the same HTML file.

3. External JavaScript
Writing JavaScript in a separate .js file and connecting it to the HTML file.

Which is best place for connect external js file head or body?
---------------------------------------------------------------


The best place to connect an external JavaScript file is usually inside the <head> tag using the defer attribute.
<script src="script.js" defer></script>

1.src="script.js" connects the external JavaScript file.

2.defer downloads the JavaScript file while HTML is being parsed and executes it after HTML parsing is complete.

3.This allows your JavaScript to access HTML elements safely.


<script src="script.js"></script>
This also works because the HTML elements are parsed before the browser executes the js script.

Difference                  Location	Recommended usage
--------------------------------------------------------------------

<head>                        with defer	Best general choice for external scripts
Before </body>	               Also a good choice for traditional scripts
<head>                        without defer	May delay HTML parsing


Notes
---------
<noscript> Tag
1. The <noscript> tag displays a message on a webpage when JavaScript is disabled in the browser.
2. The <noscript> tag does not display its message when JavaScript is enabled in the browser.



